# Two-round optimizer campaign — ready for approval

Prepared 2026-09-07T17:07:43.455885+00:00. **No external model call is authorized or has run.**

This campaign will exercise investigator → policy author → local evaluation → critic twice. Round two receives round one's actual feedback and archive. It uses the provisional S&P 500 development cohort. Successful completion demonstrates the loop; it does not establish a profitable or qualified strategy.

## What approval covers

- Model: `openai/gpt-5.4` through `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`.
- OpenRouter selects a compatible upstream. No upstream provider is pinned and upstream failover is not explicitly disabled.
- At most **2 rounds, 6 role calls, 448,000 total tokens, and 8,192 output tokens per call**, including reasoning within the output accounting. One hypothesis and at most one candidate per round.
- **No automatic retries or schema repairs.** Uncertain accepted outcomes stop for reconciliation; no blind repeat call.
- **Cost is audited; there is no enforcing USD ceiling.** At the currently published $2.50/M input and $15/M output headline rates, using the total-token ceiling with all six maximum outputs gives about **$1.73**. This is arithmetic guidance, not a guaranteed price or spending cap; routed tiers, fees and actual usage can differ. [OpenRouter pricing](https://openrouter.ai/openai/gpt-5.4).
- Each role has up to 300 seconds; each round up to 2 hours; the campaign up to 4 hours. Local evaluation: quick 600 seconds, each discovery window 1,200 seconds, one evaluator at a time.
- Use the existing `OPENROUTER` entry in the main checkout `.env`, mapped only into the launch process's `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. The key is used for API authentication, never inserted into model messages, logs or review artifacts.

## What leaves this computer

The first request contains sixteen aggregate baseline metrics and their evidence/binding identifiers. It contains no strategy source. Its exact logical request body is [initial-outbound-body.json](C:/Projects/trading_bot/RS-momentum-EMA-trading-bot/.worktrees/pit-optimizer-v5-architecture/.artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/provider-runtime-01/initial-outbound-body.json) (6,460 bytes); the conservative first-input token allowance is **10,305**, plus up to **8,192** output tokens.

Subsequent requests can send aggregate performance, predictions, typed failures, archive summaries and prior critiques. Author requests can include the editable policy sources and interface contracts for `entry.py`, `risk.py`, `position.py` and `exit.py` under `core/strategy_policy/v3/`, including all four files when the requested change crosses policies. Later request contents depend on the actual preceding results and are checked against the same cumulative caps.

Raw market/fundamental datasets, the full repository, environment values and credential-file contents are not model input. HTTP authentication uses the API key; transport metadata includes the campaign ID and request-hash prefix. JSON whitespace and HTTP headers are produced by the SDK; the saved body records the exact reviewed logical values.

